IMPORT prelude

-- Duties Act 2001 (Tas) and First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 (Tas) -- shared nouns for the seat-neutral core.
--
-- Based on material from the Tasmanian Legislation website at 20 October 2026 (State of Tasmania, CC BY 4.0). For the
-- latest information on Tasmanian Government legislation please go to www.legislation.tas.gov.au. The statutory words
-- quoted in these modules come from the unofficial plain-text deposits:
--   ../../registers/source-bundle/act-2001-015.txt (Duties Act 2001, consolidation published 2026-10-13),
--   ../../../first-home-owner-grant-act-2000/registers/source-bundle/act-2000-019.txt (consolidation published
--   2026-10-14), and
--   ../../../first-home-owner-grant-regulations-2021/registers/source-bundle/sr-2021-033.txt (published 2026-06-11).
--
-- This module holds what both Acts share: arithmetic and date helpers, the explicit "not covered" answers, the parties
-- and acts of the regulative rules, and the residence requirement, which the Duties Act (ss 46F, 57H) and the First
-- Home Owner Grant Act (s 3, s 12, s 20) state in the same words: occupy the home as a principal place of residence
-- "for a continuous period of at least 6 months ... commencing within the 12-month period immediately after" the
-- transfer or completion, and keep the interest in the land until then.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Shared nouns -- Duties Act 2001 and First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 (Tas)`

§§ `Arithmetic`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

-- s 29(1) and s 197 charge "for every $100, or part": a part of $100 counts as a whole $100.
GIVEN `amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of 100-dollar parts in` MEANS
    IF `amount` AT MOST 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF FLOOR (`amount` DIVIDED BY 100) TIMES 100 EQUALS `amount`
         THEN `amount` DIVIDED BY 100
         ELSE FLOOR (`amount` DIVIDED BY 100) PLUS 1

§§ `Dates`

-- Dates are DATE values; they are compared by their serial numbers. The stable prelude has no YMD, so a local shim.
GIVEN `y` IS A NUMBER, `m` IS A NUMBER, `d` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
YMD `y` `m` `d` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY `d` `m` `y`

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `first` IS A DATE, `last` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day falls from` `the day` `to` `first` `and` `last` IF
        DATE_SERIAL `the day` AT LEAST DATE_SERIAL `first`
    AND DATE_SERIAL `the day` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `last`

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `other` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day` `is before` `other` IF
    DATE_SERIAL `the day` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `other`

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `other` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day` `is on or after` `other` IF
    DATE_SERIAL `the day` AT LEAST DATE_SERIAL `other`

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `other` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day` `is on or before` `other` IF
    DATE_SERIAL `the day` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `other`

GIVEN `m` IS A NUMBER, `y` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the first day of the month after month` `m` `of` `y` MEANS
    IF `m` EQUALS 12
    THEN DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 (`y` PLUS 1)
    ELSE DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (`m` PLUS 1) `y`

GIVEN `m` IS A NUMBER, `y` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of days in month` `m` `of` `y` MEANS
    DATE_SERIAL (`the first day of the month after month` `m` `of` `y`) MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 `m` `y`)

-- s 242(2)-(3) (Duties Act): a period of months runs to "the end of the corresponding day of the last named month
-- within the period" or, "if there is no such corresponding day, at the end of that named month". So 3 months after
-- 30 November 2025 is 28 February 2026. READING: the same rule is used for every period of months in both Acts
-- (s 242 speaks only of when duty is due; the FHOG Act has no rule of its own), and a period "after" a day ends on
-- the corresponding day (15 March -> 15 June). A negative n counts back (6 months before a day).
GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `d` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day that is` `n` `months after` `d` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY (`the lesser of` (DATE_DAY `d`) (`the number of days in month` `the new month` `of` `the new year`)) `the new month` `the new year`
    WHERE
        `the month index` MEANS (DATE_YEAR `d` TIMES 12) PLUS (DATE_MONTH `d` MINUS 1) PLUS `n`
        `the new year`    MEANS FLOOR (`the month index` DIVIDED BY 12)
        `the new month`   MEANS `the month index` MINUS (`the new year` TIMES 12) PLUS 1

GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `d` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day that is` `n` `days after` `d` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `d` PLUS `n`)

-- Days from one day to another, for the WITHIN of a regulative rule. Traces count in days, on DATE_SERIAL numbers.
GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the first day` `until` `the second day` MEANS
    DATE_SERIAL `the second day` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the first day`

§§ `Answers outside the deposited text`

-- Where a question reaches law that the deposits do not contain, or that this baseline leaves out, the answer says so.
DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    `the transfer is dated before 21 October 2013, when the s 29 scale was last amended (No. 41 of 2013); the scale in force before then is not in the deposited consolidation`
    `a transferee is a foreign person: Part 3A additional duty for foreign purchasers (and the s 30J exemption) is not encoded`
    `the home was bought off the plan before its occupancy permit, under an agreement signed from 1 July 2024: the Division 2C pre-completion duty concession is not encoded`
    `the vehicle application is dated before 1 October 2007, when the s 197 rates were last amended (No. 18 of 2007); the rates in force before then are not in the deposited consolidation`
    `an exemption under ss 199 to 203 is claimed for the vehicle: those exemptions are not encoded`
    `the grant's commencement date is before 1 January 2013, when s 18 was substituted (No. 3 of 2013); the amount in force before then is not in the deposited consolidation`
    `the commencement date falls in a s 18A, 18B or 18C period (1 January 2013 to 31 December 2015) and the transaction is for a new home: those sections' building-commencement conditions are not encoded`
    `the grant is sought for a moveable building (s 13(6)): not encoded`

§§ `Regulative rules -- the parties and the acts`

-- The parties the two Acts name. The Commissioner of State Revenue is a party to rules, never a seat.
-- FHOG Act s 21(3): "In the case of a joint application, each applicant is individually liable to comply with a
-- requirement under subsection (2) but compliance by any one or more of them is to be regarded as compliance by both or
-- all." So the joint applicants are one party here: an act by any of them is the act of all.
DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the transferee`
    `the applicant for the grant`
    `the applicant to register the vehicle`
    `the Commissioner`

-- A stay in the home ends either way; both are read by the residence requirement below.
DECLARE `How the stay ends` IS ONE OF
    `by ceasing to occupy the home as principal place of residence`
    `by ceasing to hold the interest in the land`

-- Acts that carry a day carry it as a DATE_SERIAL number, the same number as the time of the event in a trace, so that
-- a rule that follows can count from it.
DECLARE `Duty act` IS ONE OF
    `lodge the written instrument with the Commissioner`
    `make and lodge a written statement in the approved form`
    `pay the duty`
    `begin to occupy the home as principal place of residence` HAS `on day` IS A NUMBER
    `end the stay in the home` HAS `how` IS A `How the stay ends`, `on day` IS A NUMBER
    `give the Commissioner written notice of the failure`
    `repay the grant`
    `reassess the duty as if the transaction were not an eligible transaction`
    `impose a penalty not exceeding the amount to be repaid`
    `apply for the grant`
    `apply the grant towards a liability for State taxes`
    `lodge a statement of the dutiable value with the application`

§§ `The residence requirement, shared by both Acts`

-- Duties Act s 57H(1): "If duty is not chargeable on a transfer of land in accordance with section 57G, each transferee
-- must occupy the established home situated on that land as the person's principal place of residence for a continuous
-- period of at least 6 months (or any lesser period approved by the Commissioner under subsection (2)) commencing --
-- (a) within the 12-month period immediately after the eligible transaction; or (b) within such longer period as is
-- approved by the Commissioner." (5): "each transferee must retain the person's interest in that land until the
-- residence requirement has been satisfied." (6): a transferee who fails to comply with (1) or (5) "must give written
-- notice of that fact to the Commissioner within 14 days after the failure to comply. Penalty: Fine not exceeding 100
-- penalty units." s 57I(2): the Commissioner "may reassess the duty ... as if the transaction was not an eligible
-- transaction". s 46F and s 46G(2) say the same for the Division 2A concession (transfers to 30 June 2024).
-- FHOG Act s 3 "residence requirement" and s 12(1), (3): the same, counted from "completion of the eligible
-- transaction". s 20(2)-(3): where the grant was paid in anticipation, "if the residence requirement is not complied
-- with, the applicant must within 14 days after the relevant date -- (a) give written notice of that fact to the
-- Commissioner; and (b) repay the amount of the grant"; (3A): the same within 14 days after ceasing to retain the
-- relevant interest before satisfying the requirement; (4): failure is an offence, "Fine not exceeding 100 penalty
-- units".
DECLARE `Residence provision` IS ONE OF
    `the first home buyer duty exemption (Duties Act s 57H)`
    `the first home buyer duty concession (Duties Act s 46F)`
    `a first home owner grant paid in anticipation (FHOG Act ss 12, 20)`

-- The days to give notice (and, for the grant, to repay) after a failure: 14 in each provision.
`the days to act after a failure of the residence requirement` MEANS 14

-- The defaults the text sets; the Commissioner may approve a longer period to begin and a lesser period of occupation.
`the months the text allows to begin occupying` MEANS 12
`the months of continuous occupation the text requires` MEANS 6

GIVEN `provision` IS A `Residence provision`
GIVETH A `Party`
`the party bound by` MEANS
    CONSIDER `provision`
    WHEN `a first home owner grant paid in anticipation (FHOG Act ss 12, 20)` THEN `the applicant for the grant`
    OTHERWISE `the transferee`

GIVEN `provision` IS A `Residence provision`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Duty act`
`what follows a failure under` MEANS
    CONSIDER `provision`
    WHEN `the first home buyer duty exemption (Duties Act s 57H)` THEN
            (PARTY `the transferee`
             MUST  `give the Commissioner written notice of the failure`
             WITHIN `the days to act after a failure of the residence requirement`
             LEST  BREACH BY `the transferee` BECAUSE "s 57H(6): written notice of the failure to occupy the home, or to keep the interest, must be given to the Commissioner within 14 days; fine not exceeding 100 penalty units")
        RAND
            (PARTY `the Commissioner`
             MAY   `reassess the duty as if the transaction were not an eligible transaction`)
    WHEN `the first home buyer duty concession (Duties Act s 46F)` THEN
            (PARTY `the transferee`
             MUST  `give the Commissioner written notice of the failure`
             WITHIN `the days to act after a failure of the residence requirement`
             LEST  BREACH BY `the transferee` BECAUSE "s 46F(6): written notice of the failure to occupy the home, or to keep the interest, must be given to the Commissioner within 14 days; fine not exceeding 100 penalty units")
        RAND
            (PARTY `the Commissioner`
             MAY   `reassess the duty as if the transaction were not an eligible transaction`)
    WHEN `a first home owner grant paid in anticipation (FHOG Act ss 12, 20)` THEN
            (PARTY `the applicant for the grant`
             MUST  `give the Commissioner written notice of the failure`
             WITHIN `the days to act after a failure of the residence requirement`
             LEST  BREACH BY `the applicant for the grant` BECAUSE "FHOG Act s 20(2)(a), (3A)(a), (4): written notice that the residence requirement is not met, or that the interest was given up, must be given to the Commissioner within 14 days; fine not exceeding 100 penalty units")
        RAND
            (PARTY `the applicant for the grant`
             MUST  `repay the grant`
             WITHIN `the days to act after a failure of the residence requirement`
             LEST  BREACH BY `the applicant for the grant` BECAUSE "FHOG Act s 20(2)(b), (3A)(b), (4): the grant must be repaid within 14 days; failure is an offence (fine not exceeding 100 penalty units), the Commissioner may impose a penalty up to the amount to be repaid (s 38(3)) and recover both as a debt (s 39)")

-- The days of continuous occupation, counted from the day of moving in, that end the requirement: from that day to the
-- same day `months` months later. Leaving on that later day is not a failure; leaving any earlier day is.
GIVEN `the day moved in` IS A NUMBER, `months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days of occupation required from` `the day moved in` `for` `months` MEANS
    DATE_SERIAL (`the day that is` `months` `months after` (DATE_FROM_SERIAL `the day moved in`)) MINUS `the day moved in`

-- The requirement as one rule. Times are DATE_SERIAL day numbers: `start` is the day the clock starts (the transfer,
-- or completion of the grant transaction, or a day of leaving that restarts the clock), `last day to begin` the last
-- day on which occupation may commence (12 months after the transfer or completion, or the longer period approved).
-- READING (finding 10): a person who moves in and leaves before 6 months, while the time to begin has not run out, may
-- still begin a fresh continuous period: the text requires "a continuous period of at least 6 months ... commencing
-- within" the 12 months, not that the first stay last 6 months. So leaving early restarts the rule, and is a failure
-- only once the time to begin has passed. Giving up the interest during the stay is a failure at once (s 57H(5),
-- s 46F(5), FHOG s 12(3) and s 20(3A)). LIMIT: giving up the interest before moving in is not caught by this rule
-- (the trace waits for the move); `What must I do if I gave up my interest early` in the seat answers that case.
-- `exempted` is the Commissioner's exemption of a non-complying joint transferee or applicant (s 57H(4), s 46F(4),
-- FHOG s 12(2)): the rule then binds nothing.
GIVEN `provision`         IS A `Residence provision`
      `exempted`          IS A BOOLEAN
      `start`             IS A NUMBER
      `last day to begin` IS A NUMBER
      `months to stay`    IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Duty act`
`the residence requirement under` `provision` `exempted` `start` `last day to begin` `months to stay` MEANS
    IF `exempted`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `the party bound by` `provision`
         MUST  `begin to occupy the home as principal place of residence` `the day moved in`
         WITHIN `last day to begin` MINUS `start`
         HENCE
             PARTY `the party bound by` `provision`
             DO    `end the stay in the home` `how` `the day it ends`
             WITHIN (`the days of occupation required from` `the day moved in` `for` `months to stay`) MINUS 1
             HENCE
                 CONSIDER `how`
                 WHEN `by ceasing to hold the interest in the land` THEN `what follows a failure under` `provision`
                 WHEN `by ceasing to occupy the home as principal place of residence` THEN
                     IF `the day it ends` LESS THAN `last day to begin`
                     THEN `the residence requirement under` `provision` FALSE `the day it ends` `last day to begin` `months to stay`
                     ELSE `what follows a failure under` `provision`
             LEST  FULFILLED
         LEST  `what follows a failure under` `provision`
